Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||05-15-2000||01:58 AM||||There's a vent fan for sale at my local hardware store, 1280 CFM, runs on 115v AC. I'm sure something could be rigged up with a converter or something, to get this powered from the fiero electrical system. How many lbs of boost does 1280 CFM work out to? how much air does the Fiero V6 normally take in?<P>(the fan is $70.00 CAD, from Home Hardware.)<P>speaking of fans.. DaveD mentioned putting large (computer) case fans under the decklid grills to increase cooling when a temp sensor indicated the engine compartment was too warm.. I think radiator cooling fans might work better, as they're designed to be used in a similar environment, whereas case fans are not.||||reg||1
