Z||000004||Spyder||05-15-2000||12:22 PM||||Oh No! Not again.<BR>The easiest way is to go to a place that sells boat supplies, they have some high cfm 12 volt motors. They also look like tubos.<BR>I did do this installation on my jet ski.<BR>The main thing this will do is it will be like a ram air when sitting still.<BR>Basically it’s not adding boost but making the air more available for the engine to use.<BR>Sort of like adding a K&N filter.<P>I’m sure someone will eventually make the electric blowers that have some serious boost but util then.<P>Here is my  project that I’m almost finished with:<BR>I will post the pics tomorrow.<BR>I have taken a two stroke leaf blower and added an electric start, so it doesn’t have to work all the time, no worn out  turbo bearings.  Larger fuel injectors were added to protect from a lean condition. The ECU will need an update to compensate for the additional boost.  <BR>When you are at a stop light you can turn on the “Turbo” and it will just idle, then when accelerate you  can push the turbo boost button right next to the ON  button which when pressed takes it up to full turbo boost. Sling shooting you past you adversary. <BR>Oh before I forget, I really didn’t do this modification.||||reg||1
